# Working notes at the repository root — analyses, plans, critiques, briefings,
# orchestration prompts.
#
# ⚠️ THIS IS A SAFETY PATTERN, NOT TIDINESS. The source in this repository is
# public; the planning documents that accumulate in its root are not. One that is
# untracked but NOT ignored is a single `git add -A` away from a public commit.
# That has already happened twice in spert-forecaster, caught both times only
# because someone read the file list before pushing. A near-miss caught twice by
# attention is a hazard, not a track record.
#
# Measured 2026-08-11, before this block existed: 9 such files sat in this
# repository's root and `git check-ignore` matched exactly 0 of them.
#
# ⚠️ DENY-BY-DEFAULT WITH AN ALLOWLIST — deliberately NOT a vocabulary of
# filename patterns such as `/*-CRITIQUE-*.md` or `/*-PLAN-V*.md`. Measured
# across the suite: a vocabulary tuned to one repo's naming caught 4 of another
# repo's 108 documents, because the repos name things differently
# (`NAME-CRITIQUE-v2.md` versus `CRITIQUE_name.md`). An allowlist is complete by
# construction; a vocabulary is incomplete by construction.
#
# ⚠️ A vocabulary is also SELF-FLATTERING ON A MAC, which is the part that would
# not have been noticed. APFS is case-insensitive, so `/*-PLAN-V*.md` matches
# `...-plan-v3_1.md` here and matches nothing in CI. The same block measured 16
# on macOS and 4 under `git config core.ignorecase false`. The inflation happens
# where the pattern is authored; the deflation happens where it runs.
#
# The two failure directions are not symmetrical in a public repository:
#
#   - A doc wrongly ignored is visible on GitHub and fixed by one commit. It is
#     also not silent: `git add CONTRIBUTING.md` on an ignored path exits 1 and
#     prints a hint. Only `git add -A` passes over it quietly.
#   - A planning doc wrongly committed to a public repo is not recoverable. It is
#     in the history, cloneable and indexable.
#
# ⚠️ `.gitignore` has no effect on already-tracked files, so `/*.md` does not
# untrack anything listed below and never could. The allowlist is here so that
# creating a NEW SECURITY.md or CONTRIBUTING.md is still a plain `git add`, and
# so a reader can see at a glance what this repository means to publish.
#
# Derive the allowlist, never recall it:   git ls-files ':(glob)*.md'
/*.md
!/ARCHITECTURE.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/README.md
# Conventional root docs, not present today; listed so adding one needs no edit here.
!/SECURITY.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
